<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:03Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>France: Hundreds arrested as student protests escalate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f39afb862a6d77dfdf64e0d13a8a0f1d789d2c61264d0519c9e1fc0bbb9ee398</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T23:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-as-student-protests-escalate/a-79495633--b363f8aabae5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-as-student-protests-escalate/a-79495633?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Student protests have grown in scale and intensity, with violent clashes in some places leading to hundreds of arrests and dozens of injuries.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gaza: NGO reports dire camp conditions, says Israel is moving 'Yellow Line'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af21b24524077e56d0462ab3bc75d6713645d6fa8761456f66615dffd4541f78</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T22:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gaza-ngo-reports-dire-camp-conditions-says-israel-is-moving-yellow-line/a-79488777--aae790bffc81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gaza-ngo-reports-dire-camp-conditions-says-israel-is-moving-yellow-line/a-79488777?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Danish Refugee Council alleges that Israel is employing "a policy of protracted displacement" in Gaza. It says the so-called "Yellow Line" is creeping west toward the coast, preventing many from returning home.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Five EU states plan first deportation center in Africa for 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:830d8a135813e60dc07ac08ce320123f049dffd98e96622d4cf0d78da7c2fffb</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162--dbd1d60c3bb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Greece, Germany, Austria, Denmark and the Netherlands are moving forward with plans to establish deportation centers outside the EU. An African partner country has reportedly already been selected.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Are the Houthis winning against Saudi Arabia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:292f021d259f17ad88ccc039e2dedd1dbbca9ec98551279763f7580e90b9caf6</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/are-the-houthis-winning-against-saudi-arabia/a-79492476--c9910a2a90c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/are-the-houthis-winning-against-saudi-arabia/a-79492476?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's unclear how the Saudis can defuse the threat presented by the Houthis in next-door Yemen or who they can turn to for help. The US isn't interested, the Europeans are hedging and nobody wants open conflict with Iran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's nuclear program remains shrouded in mystery as the regime debates ditching non-proliferation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99c54e810542b6321bdccfabccda4a27c4237d5bc5e43ef3dd2efe8f8be1e94e</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-nuclear-program-remains-shrouded-in-mystery-as-the-regime-debates-ditching-non-proliferation/a-79488197--eb083345c8e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-nuclear-program-remains-shrouded-in-mystery-as-the-regime-debates-ditching-non-proliferation/a-79488197?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran's nuclear program is entering a critical phase as Tehran debates dropping out of a nuclear non-proliferation treaty. Satellite images also show activity at known nuclear sites.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Lawyer of Junaid Hafeez, a Pakistai scholar imprisoned for 13 years, is hopeful for his release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abb79f23a08ff0d37d5aaf3ff596efc5111e508ae85fcb314f0fa1edad06b3b0</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207--6c93b577eab6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A former Fullbright scholar, Junaid Hafeez was sentenced to death under Pakistan's controversial blasphemy laws. His family and lawyer told DW there is now hope a court will overturn the conviction.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia elections: Polls overshadowed by exhaustion, exodus and geopolitics as ethnic politics eclipse real problems</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77285c26a0419e10ce6ddadc0c0e8f1f39f1ad78c4c9f0dbbdca7c9c596e7f69</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-elections-polls-overshadowed-by-exhaustion-exodus-and-geopolitics-as-ethnic-politics-eclipse-/a-79487802--91e658c381f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-elections-polls-overshadowed-by-exhaustion-exodus-and-geopolitics-as-ethnic-politics-eclipse-real-problems/a-79487802?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia goes to the polls on October 4 to elect several parliaments and presidents. While voters worry about the economy and emigration, the campaign is focused on ethnicity, exposing the country's political paralysis.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is US President Donald Trump right to rename AI as 'Super Intelligence'?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7857503838d074e4a2858e4806c04ebcf097435e87dcfebd6097a36a378e9471</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388--e5323453fe90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump thinks the name artificial intelligence sounds "fake" and has ordered US agencies to use "Super Intelligence" instead. Yet, tech firms and researchers have little reason to play along.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland will boycott Eurovision again because of Israel's participation, but the song contest is still expanding.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba8898ff95b4e37da6e4e1678214e861db0f7f9bd38f63b576ca659b26735726</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-stil/a-79401752--f96894bb90e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-still-expanding/a-79401752?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Eurovision Song Contest was marred by boycotts in protest against Israel's participation in the midst of its war on Gaza. It still aims to keep growing.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea: Lost shark draws over half a million visitors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4315dda5eabe3c364494e66cbd64a75c2e92517d9ced5dcfb0cb84e3c3cfe92b</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-lost-shark-draws-over-half-a-million-visitors/a-79482014--618815d2f667.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-lost-shark-draws-over-half-a-million-visitors/a-79482014?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The South Korean port of Busan says that a stranded shark has become a major tourist draw. It's also named the ocean predator an honorary ambassador to the city.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Alternative Nobel' honors women's rights activists, AI researcher</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebbd73386f441d1da028762280bfcbb0e97f087954336df91d39a95f66c7515a</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T06:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alternative-nobel-honors-women-s-rights-activists-ai-researcher/a-79481171--13d01235661c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alternative-nobel-honors-women-s-rights-activists-ai-researcher/a-79481171?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Right Livelihood Award has gone to a female AI researcher and women fighting repression. The Sweden-based prize has been dubbed an "alternative Nobel."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary's reckoning with Orban's corrupt system picks up speed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9333094e7094c43735b6c12b200f2a14c9ffc1fec9fce342af1957e0ea9cd5c</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T04:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-s-reckoning-with-orban-s-corrupt-system-picks-up-speed/a-79473714--fef6c98dbd47.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-s-reckoning-with-orban-s-corrupt-system-picks-up-speed/a-79473714?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's Prime Minister Peter Magyar vowed to dismantle Orban's corrupt networks. High-profile figures are being arrested and many Hungarians are pushing for swift accountability, but the rule of law takes time.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: No regard for civilians as fighting in Tigray continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c670622b07e066a14cb4c1c258717cbc3755ab4de2da408741233f38267417c</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-no-regard-for-civilians-as-fighting-in-tigray-continues/a-79464569--9165b7b199f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-no-regard-for-civilians-as-fighting-in-tigray-continues/a-79464569?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fighting has returned to northern Ethiopia, shattering a fragile peace in the region. DW spoke to civilians caught in the crossfire amid communication blackouts, as rebel and federal forces keep battling for territory.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
